    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "Both earlier answers remain correct and agree with their respective captured worked solutions. For q-47367, the limit at x=1 is 1, whereas f(1)=2. The function is therefore discontinuous and not differentiable at 1, making I and II false. III is true in the standard sense that differentiability on an interval requires differentiability at every point of that interval; it does not mean the function is nowhere differentiable there. For q-73260, differentiability at 4 implies continuity at 4, so I is true. A corner at 2 prevents differentiability there, so II is true. Continuity at 0 alone does not guarantee differentiability, so III is not necessarily true. No graded submissions are supplied; MA evidence comes from each question's own worked solution.",
